  "text": "Pet Chemotherapy In Dixon, IL | River Ridge Animal Hospital\n\n(815) 288-3394\nBook Appointment\nHome\nAbout\nMeet Our Team\nCareers\nTestimonials\nGallery\nPayments\nTours and Facility\nServices\nPet Preventative Health\nDog Dentistry\nPet Imaging & Labwork\nPet Pain Management\nPet Pharmacy\nView All Services\nResources\nNew Patient Center\nOnline Forms\nNew Patient Form\nCanine Boarding Admission\nFeline Boarding Admission\nDog Daycare Enrollment\nDog Daycare Agreement Form\nDog Daycare Rules and Regulations\nPet Memorial Submission\nFAQs\nAfter Hours Care\nContact\nOrder Online\nBook Appointment\n\n(815) 288-3394\nHome\nAbout\nMeet Our Team\nCareers\nTestimonials\nGallery\nPayments\nTours and Facility\nServices\nPet Preventative Health\nDog Dentistry\nPet Imaging & Labwork\nPet Pain Management\nPet Pharmacy\nView All Services\nResources\nNew Patient Center\nOnline Forms\nNew Patient Form\nCanine Boarding Admission\nFeline Boarding Admission\nDog Daycare Enrollment\nDog Daycare Agreement Form\nDog Daycare Rules and Regulations\nPet Memorial Submission\nFAQs\nAfter Hours Care\nContact\nOrder Online\nBook Appointment\nPet Chemotherapy\nManage your pet’s cancer with professional pet chemotherapy and unwavering veterinary care from\nRiver Ridge Animal Hospital\nin Dixon, IL. We offer compassionate care and advanced treatments, including chemotherapy, to monitor and treat your pet’s condition.\nBook Appointment\nThe Importance of a Pet Chemotherapy\nWhen a pet is diagnosed with cancer, it can be an emotional and overwhelming time for families. At\nRiver Ridge Animal Hospital\n, we understand the importance of providing compassionate and effective care for your pet as you face this major disease. Our\nveterinary team\nis dedicated to offering advanced treatment options, including pet chemotherapy in Dixon, IL, to help manage and treat cancer in pets.\n\nUnderstanding Pet Chemotherapy\nPet chemotherapy involves using medication to target and destroy cancer cells. This treatment can be essential in managing various types of cancers, such as lymphoma, mast cell tumors, and other malignancies. Chemotherapy can be used alone or in combination with surgery or radiation therapy, depending on the type and stage of cancer.\nOur approach to pet chemotherapy is designed to maximize the effectiveness of the treatment while minimizing side effects. We tailor each treatment plan to the specific needs of your pet, ensuring that they receive the best possible care throughout their journey.\nBenefits of Pet Chemotherapy\nChoosing chemotherapy for your pet can significantly help manage their condition, offering:\nTargeted Treatment\nChemotherapy aims to specifically target and kill cancer cells, which helps in reducing or eliminating tumors and managing cancer symptoms.\nExtended Life\nFor many pets, chemotherapy can significantly extend their quality of life and longevity by controlling cancer progression and alleviating discomfort.\nCombination Therapy\nChemotherapy can be combined with other treatments, such as surgery or radiation, to enhance overall effectiveness and provide a comprehensive approach to cancer care.\n\nWhen to Consider Pet Chemotherapy\nChemotherapy may be recommended if your pet has been diagnosed with cancer and other treatment options are either not viable or have not provided sufficient results. Common signs that may indicate the need for chemotherapy include unexplained weight loss, persistent lumps or swelling, and changes in behavior or appetite.\n\nWhy Choose River Ridge Animal Hospital?\nRiver Ridge Animal Hospital\nis dedicated to providing personalized and compassionate care for pets undergoing chemotherapy in Dixon, IL. Our experienced\nveterinary team\nis committed to delivering high-quality care while offering support and guidance throughout the treatment process. We work closely with you to develop a tailored chemotherapy plan that suits your pet’s unique needs, ensuring they receive the best possible treatment with the utmost care.\nIf your pet has been diagnosed with cancer and you are considering chemotherapy, contact us to discuss your options. We are here to support you and your pet every step of the way, offering expert care and guidance throughout the journey.\nVeterinary Services in Dixon, IL\nCat Dentistry\nDog Dentistry\nDog Daycare\nPet Boarding\nPet Chemotherapy\nPet Grooming\nPet Hospitalization\nPet Imaging & Labwork\nLaser Therapy & Surgery\nPet Memorials\nPet Pain Management\nPet Pharmacy\nPet Preventative Health\nPet Surgery\nOur Technology\nReady to Visit?\nWe proudly serve the pets of Dixon, Sterling, Rock Falls, Morrison, Amboy, Ashton, Oregon, Rochelle, IL, and the surrounding area. Feel free to visit our clinic or request an appointment by clicking the button below.\nBook an Appointment\nHave a Question?\nPlease complete our online form and a member of our team will get back to you as quickly as possible.\n\nLocation\n273 IL Route 2\nDixon, IL 61021\n\nContact Information\nPhone:\n(815) 288-3394\nFax\n: 815-288-3549\nEmail:\nstaff@riverridgevets.com\nKennel Department\nEmail:\nkennel@riverridgevets.com\n\nHours\nMonday–Friday:\n7:30 AM – 5:30 PM\nSaturday:\n7:30 AM – 12:30 PM\nSunday:\nClosed\nName\n*\nFirst\nLast\nEmail\n*\nPhone\nHow can we help you?\n*\nPhone\nSubmit\nFollow\n© 2026 River Ridge Animal Hospital |\nPowered by PetDesk\n|\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nAccessibility Statement",
